      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. If this comment is for closeSocketsForFirewallChainLocked, should we move this around that function? If not, maybe just remove the method name from comment?\ne.g.\nImmediatly closes sockets here because of the following reasons:\n...\n\n2. Since this is a long paragraph, maybe make it seasier to follow, e.g.\n\u003cAI-suggested fix\u003e\ncloseSocketsForFirewallChainLocked closes sockets immediately without delay for the following reasons:\n 1. Delaying socket closure when a firewall chain is enabled/disabled is less crucial and would make the code more complex. Changes to firewall chains occur less often than uid rule updates.\n 2. If the chain permits network access, ConnectivityService closes sockets based on uid ranges and exempt uids because it doesn\u0027t know which specific uids lose access.\n 3. Tracking reasons for closing sockets for each individual uid, uid range, and exempt uid would introduce unnecessary complexity.",
